; BossAbilities is deliberately absent, leaving it null. Do NOT reintroduce it as
; BossAbilities = Array[ExtResource("<EnemyAbilityData.cs>")]([]) -- an EMPTY typed
; array whose element type is a C# Script corrupts the Godot 4.7.1 .NET heap when
; the resource is marshalled to the EnemyAbilityData[] export, and the process dies
; later at an unrelated site. Empty arrays of builtin types (the Array[float] and
; Array[int] entries above) are safe; only Script-typed empties are fatal.
; MirrorParadoxResourceSafetyTests guards this for every enemy/boss resource.
